{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "Which skill pack (art/skills/) each weapon type's ultimate uses, and the facts of every pack: generated by tools/skills/sync_ultimates.py, do not edit the \"skills\" block by hand. To change what a weapon casts, point its entry in \"defaults\" at another skill of the same weapon_type; everything else (hit frames, range, dash, how long the move holds the fighter) follows from the pack. The packs' own rule (art/skills/ultimate_defaults.json) is that an ultimate always strikes FORWARD, never around the user. body_length_m = 1 body length in game (the chibi's 1.5067 m without hair x its 1.128 scale); a pack's range_body_lengths times that is how far the move reaches. min_active_ticks is the shortest hit window a pack with a single hit event gets (a one-tick window would be unfair to aim). dash_front_body_lengths is how far past the landing point a forward_dash pack still hits (its box covers the ground it crossed). defaults: the weapon has no element in the item catalog yet, so the pack is chosen to match the weapon's skill_names in weapons.json; by_element is ready for the day items carry an element (element -> pack, per weapon type). camera (per skill): what the player's camera does while that ultimate is cast, read from the pack (see the CAMERA notes in tools/skills/sync_ultimates.py) and played by client/ultimate_camera.gd: keys = shots on the clip's time (game = the player's chosen angle, frame = camera and aim in the caster's frame [right, up, forward] in pack metres, orbit = the chosen angle turned yaw_deg round the caster), shakes, an optional darker view tone. source default = the pack brings no camera: one small shake (camera_default) on its last hit. Special shots are PvE-only and owner-only. The art packs (art/skills/) were deleted with the old skill system (class-skills.md, Boss 2026-11-13): folder/presentation are dropped; the numbers stay for the classic weapon ultimates.",
